            <ArticleTitle>Monosymptomatic hypochondriasis, abnormal illness behaviour and suicide.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>475-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two cases of chronic monosymptomatic psychogenic eye pain with abnormal illness behaviour are presented. Both failed to respond to a wide variety of treatments, and despite the accepted low suicidal risk in hypochondriasis both killed themselves. The origin, prognosis and therapy of such behaviour are discussed in this context.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
